# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sched-2 window (the admission levers; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sched-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-2 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-sched-2/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the
# same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone.
# C1 (TIMED, the CONTROL of the first ABAB pair): the ship-5 candidate c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5 on Swift, the stack production runs.
# Tests: warmup; concurrent8_steady (eight fresh prompts of ~3.5k tokens together into a FRESH process, right after the warmup: every one of the eight slots is new, so the
# ledger's bracket and the conv-slice readback are paid eight times; the last first token is 15.4 s at ship 5 and the engine builds are 497 / 736 / 622 / 640 / 556 / 557 /
# 598 / 522 ms); agent_turns (six sessions of 64k-200k tokens that return twelve times: the returning-turn first token is p50 1.46 s / p90 2.33 s). Every boot a fresh
# reset. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. READ: READ the arm with
# python3 scripts/ci/sched2_report.py <arm container log> --second <control container log> (and --burst for the first eight fresh prompts, one line an arrival): the serial
# chain (hold + drain + bind) of returning turns and of fresh prompts, the bind's parts (A, B, C and C's phases), the ledger bracket and the conv-slice readback (only at a
# slot's first use), the seed first lines (deferred, bound in the sampler and why, how long the first token left ahead of the bind), the hold reuse lines (how many holds
# took no allocator reading, their age). Every figure prints "-" when no line is behind it. The model of the same arithmetic is python3 scripts/ci/sched2_model.py
# (ESTIMATES: docs/tp4-sched2.md section 5). CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models
# answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through
# the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the
# lever. Duration (estimate): 35 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=80
